About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

Our&nbsp; Policy and Economics practice is looking for an experienced Consultant or Senior Consultant to join the team. &nbsp;

We support clients from policy develo pment to delivery and capital deployment , from regulatory strategies to business case submissions, and from competition cases to expert opinion . Our economists, policy specialists, regulatory experts and techno-economic modellers work alongside governments, regulators, investors and corporates - shaping regulatory and policy frameworks , as well as decisions , which underpin multi-billion-pound investment across energy, utilities and wider infrastructure.

What you will be doing

• Apply economic reasoning and quantitative analysis to assess the impact of policy and regulatory changes on energy markets, investors,&nbsp; consumers and other market participants.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Develop robust analytical models and&nbsp; evidence -based insights to inform client decision-making on complex policy and market issues.&nbsp;

• Translate technical analysis into clear, compelling and commercially relevant recommendations for clients.

• Produce high-quality written outputs, including reports, presentations and briefing materials for senior client stakeholders.

• Contribute to business development activities, including proposal writing, discussions on client propositions, and the development of new service offerings.&nbsp;

• Build trusted relationships with clients and support the delivery of projects from inception through to final recommendations.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Contribute to internal initiatives that strengthen the team's capabilities, analytical tools, intellectual property and market profile.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Stay abreast of emerging policy, regulatory and market developments, identifying implications for clients and opportunities for new work.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;

&nbsp;
