Job Description:

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Lead solution design from business problem to target architecture, integration and deployment blueprint. &nbsp;

• Design single and multi-agent workflows, tool calling, memory, retrieval and human-in-the-loop controls. &nbsp;

• Define security, resilience, latency, cost, observability and scalability requirements. &nbsp;

• Select models, cloud services, vector search and frameworks; assess build versus buy. &nbsp;

• Set standards and guardrails, review designs, and partner with product, cloud and AI governance. &nbsp;

• Embed AIDLC in design: stage gates, governance checkpoints and architecture decision records. &nbsp;

Must-Have Skills &nbsp;

• Architecture: Architecture and distributed systems; hands-on software engineering; secure cloud architecture; API, data and identity integration. &nbsp;

• Agentic AI: LLM, RAG and agentic patterns; tool calling, state and memory; agent evaluation; build-versus-buy trade-offs. &nbsp;

• Security (banking-critical): Least-privilege tool access; prompt-injection defence; approval gates for risky actions; audit trails, model risk and residency. &nbsp;

• AIDLC (mandatory): Defines AIDLC stages and gates; evaluation and release criteria; governance checkpoints; architecture decision records. &nbsp;

Good-to-Have Skills &nbsp;

• LangGraph, Semantic Kernel, AutoGen. &nbsp;

• Enterprise search and vector databases. &nbsp;

• Event-driven systems and microservices. &nbsp;

• Red-teaming and LLM observability. &nbsp;

• Model governance and AI safety. &nbsp;

• Disaster recovery and FinOps modelling. &nbsp;

Location: Remote, UK-based. Roughly 80% remote, 10% office (Basingstoke), 10% on-site (global travel)

Contract: Full-Time, Fixed-Term - 12 Months

Travel: Some global travel to Cricket-playing nations (travel, accommodation and daily living allowance expenses paid by Hawk-Eye)

Expected Start Date: Summer 2027

WHY HAWK-EYE & WHY IHAWK?

Join us at Hawk-Eye and be part of an exhilarating journey in the world of Cricket. Our iHAWK product is a lightweight ball-tracking solution, usually worn on the body of the umpire. This product allows huge levels of versatility due to its size and ability for the video to be tracked remotely from anywhere in the world. From training sessions with IPL franchises to international matches with the England team, the system has been tried and tested in a wide range of scenarios.

As an iHawk Systems Operator, you will be delivering our world-renowned ball-tracking and player analysis system and providing other officiating and broadcast-enhancing technologies at cricket events both remotely and around the world. This role provides a genuine opportunity to create a direct impact on the biggest occasions and moments in cricket; this could be providing the data that leads to a player's selection for an international side, or offering broadcast analysis at a cricket World Cup.

Our powerful hardware and software will allow your creativity to flourish, with ideas and innovation being the main tools behind our success. You will get the opportunity to work with passionate, innovative, motivated and intelligent people throughout the company, who will continually try to push your personal development and engage with your desired career path.

WHAT DOES AN IHAWK SYSTEMS OPERATOR DO?

A typical day will vary, based on the different projects you could be involved in. Typically, you’ll be:

- Tracking sessions remotely, both live and retrospectively;

- Being the key point of contact for analysts and providing remote support;

- Working with developers to test software elements of the system and offer improvements;

- Building and maintenance of kits in the office;

- Going away to install broadcast services and permanent installations for cricket boards.

As part of our team, you’ll take on a central role in ensuring smooth, accurate tracking of sessions, whether monitoring them live or reviewing them retrospectively. You'll be the key contact for our analysts, offering guidance and solutions remotely to ensure they can work seamlessly.

In collaboration with our talented developers, you’ll help test and refine software components, suggesting improvements to enhance system performance. Your hands-on skills will also come into play as you build and maintain kits in the office, keeping our equipment ready for action.

This role has a dynamic, on-the-go element, too! You’ll occasionally travel to set up for cricket boards, manage broadcasts, and handle installations, assisting the full lifecycle of our innovative systems on-site.

WHY IS THIS THE RIGHT JOB FOR YOU?

This position is perfect for you if you possess:

- A technical grounding;

- Strong problem-solving skills;

- Excellent communication with the ability to liaise with clients and customers in a professional and approachable manner;

- Great teamwork skills;

- A passion for innovation;

- A willingness to learn;

- Flexible and willing to travel worldwide;

- The ability to thrive in a fast-paced and pressurised environment;

- An interest in the sport of Cricket;

- Must be currently studying towards an undergraduate degree.

At Hawk-Eye Innovations, we appreciate and value the importance of potential and growth. If you believe that you excel in certain areas and possess the passion and desire to develop further, we encourage you to apply.

